## 6. Compliance

### [BPR-COMPLIANCE] Compliance criteria — machine signal + glass gate per requirement

| ID | Requirement | Machine criterion | Glass / integration gate |
|----|-------------|-------------------|--------------------------|
| BPR-C1 | Pull-initiated only | edge netns opens no peer/sync listener; master->edge connect refused | network-architect signs zero-inbound firewall1 matrix |
| BPR-C2 | Critical propagate-or-degrade | dropped-hop test: ack-or-fault; silent-clear count = 0 | severed-link reviewer sees ack-or-fault on origin |
| BPR-C3 | Subscription-scoped mirror + lazy fetch | only subscribed namespaces mirrored; body fetched once then cached; absent -> `unresolved` | — |
| BPR-C4 | Tolerate link-down + converge | sever/restore: apps functional on cache; zero lost critical-acks | reviewer observes edge stays live during outage |
| BPR-C5 | Auth independent of network trust | non-ACL peer rejected at connect, no partial mirror | network-architect confirms Tailscale ACL tag scope |
| BPR-C6 | One multiplexed channel | one outbound endpoint carries read/write/sync/fetch; substream backpressure isolates critical from bulk | — |
| BPR-C7 | Relay provenance / actuation quarantine | relayed control does not actuate mock actuator without opt-in | reviewer confirms no unintended actuation across the peer |
| BPR-C8 | CAN-ID<->namespace mapping (Slice B) | prefix sub -> one acceptance mask; round-trip identity; unmapped -> fault | — |
| BPR-C9 | Fragmentation/reassembly (Slice B) | byte-identical reassembly; lost fragment -> fault, no partial | — |
| BPR-C10 | Synthesize-or-degrade CAN semantics (Slice B) | critical-ack confirmed via type-8 frame or fault; no fabricated `ok` | reviewer sees device actuate-with-ack or a raised fault |
| BPR-C11 | Unified Transport contract ([BPR-TRANSPORT-CONTRACT]) | both poles satisfy the one `Transport` waist + declare a `TransportProfile`; egress = fire-and-forget (never touches ack machinery); bridge = critical-ack (silent-clear = 0) | — |

- part-of: [SPEC:CIO-BUS-PEER]

